-**Known limitation.** `resume` on a migrated task fails with
-`extension_version_mismatch: <w> has no recorded store helper for this task` —
-`apply` drops the helper half of the pin (a separate recorded defect, not this
-command's doing). The remedy is `autosk enroll <task> --workflow <w>` (lands
-on the workflow's first step; `--step` names another) and then `resume`; the
-task continues on the migrated distribution.
+- the reverse plan hits any of the planner refusals listed for
+  `plan`/`apply` above, evaluated on the reverse direction (the original's
+  `to` as source, the original's `from` as target) — including unrecorded
+  distributions, stranded or unreadably pinned tasks, split workflow pins
+  and split source documents.
+
+The store itself can still decline an apply, rollback or continuation:
+
+- the plan names no tasks — `migration names no tasks` (checked before
+  any receipt is written: nothing is written, so no receipt stays open);
+- a task was re-pinned or unpinned since the receipt opened — `migration
+  <id>: <task> is no longer pinned to <from>, refusing to continue`;
+- a task's pin document no longer matches the receipt's claim — `migration
+  <id>: <task> came from document <d>, and the receipt claims <d'>`;
+- a task did not read back on the target — `migration <id>: <task> did not
+  read back on <to>`;
+- a task read back on the wrong document — `migration <id>: <task> read
+  back on document <d>, expected <d'>`;
+- a task read back on the wrong shape — `migration <id>: <task> read back
+  on shape <g>, expected <g'>`;
+- a task already on the target has no helper snapshot to check against —
+  `migration <id>: <task> is already on <to> and nothing predating the
+  write records the helper it should carry`;
+- a task read back on the wrong store helper — `migration <id>: <task>
+  read back on store helper <h>, expected <h'>`;
+- a re-opened receipt disagrees with how it was opened — `migration <id>
+  was opened with <field> <old> and is now asked for <new>` (raised when
+  the open receipt is re-checked, not while a task moves).
+
+Every decline above but `migration names no tasks` leaves the receipt
+open, and the next `apply` continues the same migration once the cause is
+removed.
 
